      "content": "It's important to clarify that there's no scientific basis for the idea of an \"aura\" that can disrupt physical environments. Emotions and internal states don't interact with the physical world in the way you're describing. It's entirely natural that intense emotions can make you highly aware of your surroundings, but they can't literally cause electrical or structural changes in your office.\n\nIf you're interested in exploring this concept as a metaphor for your psychological or emotional state, it might certainly provide a unique angle for self-reflection or creative endeavors. Embracing art, creative writing, or expressive activities could serve as healthy outlets for your intense feelings.\n\nTo address your immediate concerns, though, working on communication and stress-relief techniques like deep breathing, meditation, or even physical exercise can be helpful. And, to ensure there are no underlying technical issues, it would be wise to arrange a meeting with your workspace's facilities team for an inspection. Keep communicating openly with your employer about your workplace experiences, either regarding your emotional state or any potential safety concerns, so you can find solutions together.",
